# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: PrisonArc | Scene: PrisonPath1

translate zh strings:

    old "I don't want to answer any of your questions. We're done talking."
    new "我不想回答你的任何问题。我们谈完了。"

    old "The guard captain looked at her for what seemed like almost a minute."
    new "队长盯着她，那目光似乎持续了将近一分钟。"

    old "Then he shrugged."
    new "然后他耸了耸肩。"

    old "Fine, do it your way."
    new "好吧，按你的方式来。"

    old "The captain leaned back in his chair and knocked the wall."
    new "队长往椅背上一靠，敲了敲墙壁。"

    old "Suddenly, the door the room flew open."
    new "突然，房间的门猛地被推开。"

    old "Marching into the room, two guards, carrying between them..."
    new "两名守卫大步走进房间，合力抬着……"

    old "He looked battered and bruised. They'd clearly given him a rougher time than her."
    new "他看起来伤痕累累，青一块紫一块的。显然，他们对他比对她更狠。"

    old "Sarah tried to look into his eyes, but his eyes were fixed on the ground."
    new "莎拉试图看向他的眼睛，但他的目光却死死盯着地面。"

    old "So, guess it's your lucky day ya worthless piece of shit."
    new "看来今天是你走运的日子，你这毫无价值的废物。"

    old "Girly here is pretending like she don't know shit about shit, so the first one to speak gets the prize."
    new "这丫头片子装得跟什么都不懂似的，那第一个开口的就得受罚。"

    old "Two weeks in a work house."
    new "两周苦役。"

    old "The last one to speak gets five years housing and food, courtesy of the Lethram prison system."
    new "最后一个开口的，要判五年监禁，食宿由莱瑟拉姆监狱系统提供。"

    old "Sarah was still trying to process what was happening."
    new "莎拉还在努力消化眼前发生的一切。"

    old "Alaric was faster."
    new "阿拉里克更快。"

    old "His face shot up and he looked directly at her."
    new "他猛地抬起头，直直地看向她。"

    old "She!"
    new "是她！"

    old "It was her idea, all of it!"
    new "全是她的主意，全都是！"

    old "She made me do it, I swear!"
    new "是她逼我这么做的，我发誓！"

    old "Sarah felt her chest tighten, her breath escaped her."
    new "莎拉感到胸口发紧，呼吸变得急促。"

    old "What was happening."
    new "究竟发生了什么。"

    old "And you'll testify to this in a court?"
    new "你会在法庭上为此作证吗？"

    old "Yes! Yes! I'll say whatever you need me to say, it's all true!"
    new "对！对！你要我说什么我就说什么，全都是真的！"

    old "Good, take em back and give a nice meal and a warm bath."
    new "好，把他带回去，给他弄顿好吃的，再让他洗个热水澡。"

    old "The guards turned around and took Alaric away."
    new "卫兵们转过身，将阿拉里克带了下去。"

    old "Sarah could not bring herself to believe it."
    new "莎拉无法相信自己竟然会遭遇这种事。"

    old "Alaric...had betrayed her. And it hadn't even taken him more than a second to make up his mind."
    new "阿拉里克……背叛了她。而他甚至没有花超过一秒钟的时间来下定决心。"

    old "She didn't know this man at all."
    new "她根本不了解这个男人。"

    old "She was nothing to her, just some random girl he'd met and gotten caught up with. Of course he'd sell her out to save his life."
    new "她对他来说什么都不是，不过是他偶然遇到并卷入其中的某个普通女孩罢了。当然，为了保命，他肯定会出卖她。"

    old "Stupid. How could she have been so stupid to put her trust in a man she barely knew."
    new "愚蠢。她怎么能如此愚蠢，竟会信任一个几乎不了解的男人。"

    old "Captain...please, if you'll allow me to explain-"
    new "上尉……求您了，如果您能让我解释一下——"

    old "He waved his hands, dismissing her."
    new "他挥了挥手，示意她不必再说了。"

    old "I got all I need, girly."
    new "我需要的信息都齐了，小姑娘。"

    old "Our star witness just fingered you for the whole operation, and like I said, him or you, I'm fine with it either way."
    new "我们的头号证人指认你策划了整起行动，就像我说的，无论是他坐牢还是你进去，我都无所谓。"

    old "I tried to be nice to you, give you the first crack at it, but you wanted to play like a tough criminal."
    new "我本想对你客气点，给你个从轻发落的机会，可你偏要装成个硬茬罪犯。"

    old "So sure, you wanna pretend to be a real criminal, then you can enjoy a few years up in Lethram prison, with the other real criminals."
    new "好啊，既然你想装成真正的罪犯，那就去莱瑟姆监狱待上几年，跟那些真正的罪犯作伴吧。"

    old "He leaned over across the table."
    new "他俯身越过桌子。"

    old "But if I'm being honest, and I hate to be the one to break it to you, but a girl like you..."
    new "但说实话，我也不想这样打击你，可像你这样的女孩……"

    old "You're about two clicks too soft for a place like that."
    new "你太嫩了点，去那种地方可不够格。"

    old "Those women are gonna eat you alive."
    new "那些女人会把你生吞活剥的。"

    old "But whatever. I gave you a chance and you spat in my face. You made your bed, now you get to lie in it."
    new "不过算了。我给了你机会，你却当面吐口水侮辱我。你自己选的这条路，就自己受着吧。"

    old "Sarah could feel the tears begin to stream past her face."
    new "莎拉能感觉到泪水开始顺着她的脸颊滑落。"

    old "She opened her mouth, only to realize that there were no words."
    new "她张开嘴，却发觉无话可说。"

    old "There were no words that would save her."
    new "没有任何话语能救她。"

    old "Only a few hours later, Sarah was brought before a judge in the Lethram courthouse."
    new "几个小时后，莎拉被带到莱瑟拉姆法院的法官面前。"

    old "They sat her down on the front bench, still tied up."
    new "他们让她坐在前排的长椅上，她仍然被绑着。"

    old "We begin case 27442-yz, theft and conspiracy, each one count."
    new "我们开始审理第27442-yz号案件，涉及盗窃和共谋罪，每项指控分别计。"

    old "What evidence does the city guard offer up?"
    new "城卫队提供了什么证据？"

    old "The guard captain stepped forward."
    new "卫队长走上前。"

    old "Your honour, we provide several written accounts of patrons at the marketplace where the offense took place."
    new "大人，我们提供了案发时市场内多名顾客的书面证词。"

    old "In addition, we provide testimony from the co-conspirator of the defendant. He took part in her crimes, but she was the main instigator."
    new "此外，我们提供了被告同伙的证词。他参与了她的罪行，但她是主要的煽动者。"

    old "The judge received the papers and went through them."
    new "法官接过文件，仔细翻阅起来。"

    old "After a moment of deliberation, he finally spoke."
    new "片刻的沉思后，他终于开口了。"

    old "The court of Lethram finds this evidene compelling. Does the defendant wish to offer up any counter evidence?"
    new "雷瑟拉姆法庭认为这些证据具有说服力。被告是否希望提出任何反证？"

    old "Sarah was pulled up to her feet by a guard."
    new "一名卫兵将莎拉拉了起来。"

    old "Your honour...I...I didn't-"
    new "法官大人……我……我没——"

    old "The judge waved his hands, silencing her."
    new "法官挥了挥手，让她噤声。"

    old "Please, the current state of prosecution does not permit oral testimony."
    new "请，目前的检方状况不允许口头证词。"

    old "Do you offer up any concrete evidence for this court to review?"
    new "你能为法庭提供什么具体的证据来审查？"

    old "I...your honour...I didn't have time to-"
    new "我……法官大人……我没时间——"

    old "Again, he bade her to be silent with a gesture."
    new "再次，他用手势示意她保持沉默。"

    old "Very well, then this court has seen enough."
    new "既然如此，本庭已听够了。"

    old "The totality of the evidence leans towards guilt, and so the court finds defendant guilty of one count of theft and one count of conspiracy."
    new "综合所有证据，法庭认定被告犯有一项盗窃罪和一项共谋罪。"

    old "Punishment for each count is three years, for a total of six years in prison."
    new "每项指控的刑罚为三年，总计六年监禁。"

    old "Given that this is defendants first criminal account, we shall strike one year from the total sentence, for a total of five years in prison."
    new "鉴于这是被告的首次犯罪记录，我们将从总刑期里减去一年，最终判处五年监禁。"

    old "The judge grabbed his gavel."
    new "法官握紧了手中的法槌。"

    old "Then he brought it down with a hard strike against the bench."
    new "随后，他用力将法槌敲在审判台上。"

    old "Verdict has been rendered and spoken."
    new "判决已作出并宣读。"

    old "Guards, you may enact the pronounced punishment effective immediatly. Please take the defendant to the Lethram women's prison."
    new "卫兵，你们可以立即执行已宣判的刑罚。请将被告带往莱瑟拉姆女子监狱。"

    old "Sarah felt her body shake as they seized her upper arms and dragged her along."
    new "莎拉感到自己的身体在颤抖，当他们抓住她的上臂并拖拽着她前行时。"

    old "That was it, she realized."
    new "她终于明白了。"

    old "Less than five minutes and they had convicted her to five years in prison."
    new "不到五分钟，他们便判了她五年监禁。"

    old "She prayed it wasn't happening, but still, it did."
    new "她祈祷这一切不是真的，但事实却偏偏如此。"

    old "Sarah felt the world fade around her as they dragged her to the cart."
    new "莎拉感到周围的世界正在消退，他们把她拖向马车。"

    old "Before long, they arrived at the gates of the Lethram women's prison."
    new "没过多久，他们便抵达了莱瑟姆女子监狱的大门。"

    old "The guards put her in a room, then left."
    new "守卫把她关进一间屋子，然后离开了。"

    old "For the first time, she was alone."
    new "这是她第一次独自一人。"

    old "Sitting there, Sarah tried to process what had all happened."
    new "坐在那里，莎拉试图理清刚刚发生的一切。"

    old "Not even a day had gone by since she woke up in the alley, and now she was here..."
    new "距离她在那个巷子里醒来甚至还没过一天，现在她却身处此地……"

    old "Alone again. Betrayed for a second time."
    new "再次孤身一人。第二次遭到背叛。"

    old "What friends did she have left, she wondered, that might care to save her?"
    new "她心想，自己还剩下哪些朋友可能会在乎并来救她呢？"

    old "She knew the answer. None."
    new "她心里清楚答案：一个也没有。"

    old "Part of her wanted to cry, but another part of her knew she had to be strong."
    new "她的一部分想哭，但另一部分她知道必须坚强。"

    old "Sarah knew she had to force herself to be strong if she wanted to survive this."
    new "莎拉知道，若想活下来，她必须强迫自己坚强起来。"

    old "Suddenly, the door flew open and a man marched in, breaking whatever silence Sarah had enjoyed for a moment."
    new "突然，门被猛地推开，一个男人大步走了进来，打破了莎拉刚刚享受到的片刻宁静。"

    old "Up on your feet, prisoner."
    new "站起来，囚犯。"

    old "Sarah did as she was ordered."
    new "莎拉照命令做了。"

    old "She saw him looking at her, surprised for a moment, as if he couldn't believe she was here."
    new "她看见他正看着她，有一瞬间的惊讶，仿佛不敢相信她就在这里。"

    old "Neither could Sarah."
    new "莎拉也无法相信。"

    old "Newbie?"
    new "新手？"

    old "I'm sorry?"
    new "什么？"

    old "I mean, are you new? First time in the system?"
    new "我是说，你是新手吗？第一次进入这个系统？"

    old "Alright then."
    new "好吧。"

    old "Well my name is Matthew, but you can call me officer Matt, got that?"
    new "我叫马修，不过你可以叫我马特警官，听明白了吗？"

    old "And your name, inmate?"
    new "那你的名字呢，犯人？"

    old "Sarah...sir."
    new "莎拉……长官。"

    old "Sarah...alright. Nice name, but for the duration of your stay your name will be inmate-2244, got it?"
    new "莎拉……行吧。名字不错，但在你服刑期间，你的编号是囚犯2244，听明白了吗？"

    old "Even her name they would take from her."
    new "就连她的名字，他们也要从她身上夺走。"

    old "I'm head jailer for the west-wing section, which is where you'll be put up."
    new "我是西翼区的典狱长，你将被关押在那里。"

    old "Western wing is burglars, thieves, counterfeiters, the usual types of asset offenses."
    new "西翼关的是入室盗窃、扒手和伪造者，也就是那些常见的财产类罪犯。"

    old "No killers, those are in east-wing, so lucky you I suppose."
    new "没有杀人犯，那些人在东翼，所以算你走运了。"

    old "Sarah wasn't sure if she should smile back, but decided to do it regardless."
    new "莎拉不确定是否该回以微笑，但还是决定这么做。"

    old "I like my part of the prison nice and clean."
    new "我喜欢我负责的这片区域保持整洁干净。"

    old "That means no fights. No drugs. No trouble."
    new "这意味着不准打架，不准吸毒，不准惹事。"

    old "You keep to that, you won't get no trouble with me."
    new "只要你守规矩，我就不会找你麻烦。"

    old "You decide to fuck around...well, let's just assume that you won't do that, alright?"
    new "你要是敢耍花样……好吧，咱们就假设你不会那么做，行吗？"

    old "Yes...sir, I won't cause you any trouble."
    new "是的……先生，我不会给您惹麻烦的。"

    old "Matthew nodded."
    new "马修点了点头。"

    old "Good, that's what I like to hear."
    new "很好，这正是我想听到的。"

    old "Matthew looked at the sheet of paper in his hand, checking off the boxes."
    new "马修看着手中的那张纸，勾选着上面的方框。"

    old "Alright then, intake, gonna need all your items."
    new "好吧，接下来是登记程序，我需要你交出所有的随身物品。"

    old "Sarah reached into her pockets and emptied them out on the table next to her."
    new "莎拉把手伸进口袋，把里面的东西都掏出来放在旁边的桌子上。"

    old "Matthew laughed."
    new "马修笑了。"

    old "That's a decent start."
    new "这算是个不错的开始。"

    old "But I'm really talking about ALL your items."
    new "不过我说的可是你所有的东西。"

    old "It took a moment before it dawned on Sarah what he meant."
    new "莎拉过了片刻才明白他的意思。"

    old "Her face turned red."
    new "她的脸红了。"

    old "Can I get dressed somewhere in private?"
    new "我能找个私密的地方穿衣服吗？"

    old "Matthew shook his head."
    new "马修摇了摇头。"

    old "No, sorry. Policy states we need to be present for prisoner intake."
    new "不行，抱歉。规定要求我们在接收囚犯时必须在场。"

    old "You wouldn't believe the types of contraband that some prisoners try to smuggle in."
    new "你不会相信有些囚犯试图走私进来的违禁品都有些什么。"

    old "And it's for your safety too. Make sure nobody is bringing in any weapons."
    new "这也是为了你的安全着想。确保没有人带进任何武器。"

    old "You understand, right?"
    new "你明白的，对吧？"

    old "Sarah gritted her teeth, but she also knew she had no power here."
    new "莎拉咬紧牙关，但她清楚自己在这里毫无还手之力。"

    old "Sliding her hands under the straps of her dress, she began to slowly take it off."
    new "她将双手伸到连衣裙的肩带下方，开始慢慢脱下衣服。"

    old "She could see from the corner of her eyes that Matthew's eyes were fixed on her body."
    new "她眼角瞥见，马修的目光紧紧锁在她的身体上。"

    old "It was obvious to her that there was more than professional interest here."
    new "她很清楚，这里头除了职业兴趣之外，还有别的东西。"

    old "She took off her dress and began to fold it, putting it next to the items on the table."
    new "她脱下连衣裙，开始将其折叠好，放在桌上其他物品旁边。"

    old "Matthew gestured at her body."
    new "马修朝她的身体做了个手势。"

    old "All of it, inmate."
    new "全部，囚犯。"

    old "Sarah wanted to yell at him, but it would make no difference."
    new "莎拉本想冲他大喊，但这毫无意义。"

    old "Once she had imagined only her future husband would see this part of her."
    new "曾经，她只想象过自己的未来丈夫会看到她的这一面。"

    old "Sarah reached behind, unclasping her bra and throwing it onto the table."
    new "莎拉伸手到背后，解开胸罩的搭扣，将其扔在桌上。"

    old "Sliding her hands past her hips, she took off her panties and finally dropped the last item of clothing on the table."
    new "她将双手滑过臀部，脱下内裤，终于将最后一件衣物扔在了桌上。"

    old "Standing so naked in the room, Sarah felt very vulnerable."
    new "就这样赤身裸体地站在房间里，莎拉感到十分脆弱。"

    old "She covered up her breasts with one arm, covering up her sex with the other hand."
    new "她用一只手臂遮住胸部，另一只手遮住私处。"

    old "She could see Matthew's eyes gliding up and down her body."
    new "她能感觉到马修的目光在她身上上下打量。"

    old "Good. Turn around for me."
    new "很好。转过去面对我。"

    old "Now facing the wall, she couldn't see him, but she could feel his eyes on her back."
    new "现在背对着墙，她看不见他，却能感觉到他的目光落在她的背上。"

    old "It was humiliating."
    new "这令人屈辱。"

    old "Good, turn around and face me, inmate."
    new "好，转过身来面对我，囚犯。"

    old "He walked up close to her and suddenly grabbed her by the chin."
    new "他走近她，突然捏住了她的下巴。"

    old "Open wide, inmate."
    new "张大嘴，囚犯。"

    old "Sarah opened her mouth."
    new "莎拉张开了嘴。"

    old "Matthew craned his head from side to side, looking into her mouth."
    new "马修侧着头，向她的嘴里看去。"

    old "Alright, no contraband there."
    new "好了，里面没有违禁品。"

    old "Go ahead and sit on the edge of the table for me."
    new "去，坐在桌子边上。"

    old "You questioning me, inmate?"
    new "你在质问我吗，囚犯？"

    old "No...I just..."
    new "不……我只是……"

    old "Cause I told you, that aught to be good enough reason for you. Now sit on the edge of the table."
    new "因为我告诉过你，这对你来说应该已经是足够的理由了。现在坐到桌子边缘去。"

    old "Spread your legs."
    new "把腿分开。"

    old "Matthew quickly closed the distance between them, grabbing her upper legs and forcefully spreading them apart."
    new "马修迅速缩短了两人之间的距离，抓住她的双腿大腿处，强行将她们分开。"

    old "Prison protocol for intake states a full cavity check as part of proper procedure."
    new "监狱的入监规程规定，作为标准程序的一部分，必须对体腔进行彻底检查。"

    old "Prisoners come in here hiding all sorts of things up in whatever parts they can come up with."
    new "犯人进来时，总喜欢把各种东西藏在她们能想到的任何部位里。"

    old "So spread em, or I'll get some extra men in here and we'll do it real proper."
    new "所以把腿张开，不然我就叫几个兄弟进来，咱们按规矩好好办。"

    old "Sarah was close to screaming at him, but again, she swallowed her pride."
    new "莎拉几乎要对他尖叫，但这一次，她咽下了自尊。"

    old "She turned her face away from him and spread her legs apart."
    new "她转过头去，不再看他，并将双腿分开。"

    old "From the corner of her eyes she could see him bend down on his knees, looking directly between her legs."
    new "她用眼角余光瞥见，他双膝跪地俯下身来，目光直勾勾地盯着她两腿之间。"

    old "She felt a shock run through her body as two of his fingers entered into her."
    new "当他的两根手指进入她体内时，一股战栗感传遍了她全身。"

    old "A small yelp slipped past her lips and she gripped the edge of the table."
    new "一声轻呼从她唇间溢出，她紧紧抓住了桌沿。"

    old "Sorry, procedure you know."
    new "抱歉，你知道的，这是程序。"

    old "Sarah dug her fingers deeper into the edge of the table, the alternative was punching him."
    new "莎拉将手指更深地抠进桌沿，否则她真想揍他一顿。"

    old "She felt his fingers slide out from between her legs."
    new "她感觉到他的手指从两腿间抽了出去。"

    old "Great, no contraband."
    new "很好，没有违禁品。"

    old "Just the last check and we're done."
    new "就最后检查一遍，然后我们就结束。"

    old "Matthew made a spinning motion."
    new "马修做了一个转身的动作。"

    old "Go ahead and turn around for me."
    new "转过身去。"

    old "Alright, now bend over on the desk and grab the edges real right."
    new "好，现在趴在桌子上，双手紧紧抓住桌沿。"

    old "Again, Sarah obeyed his instructions."
    new "莎拉再次听从了他的指令。"

    old "Some women tell me this hurts, but ya know, others are fine with it. I guess it's a matter of how experienced they are with it."
    new "有些女人告诉我这很疼，但你知道的，其他人倒觉得没事。我想这跟她们这方面的经验有关吧。"

    old "Sarah felt a sharp pain explode from her ass."
    new "莎拉感到一阵剧痛从她的屁股炸开。"

    old "She nearly lost her balance, tipping over and falling onto her elbows."
    new "她差点失去平衡，身子一歪，重重地摔在肘部上。"

    old "She could feel one of Matt's hands on the back of her hand, keeping her pinned down."
    new "她能感觉到马特的一只手按在她手背上，将她牢牢按住。"

    old "The other hand was near her ass, one finger plunged deeply into her asshole."
    new "另一只手在她屁股旁，一根手指深深插入了她的肛门。"

    old "The pain roared from her lower body, and in its wake, a deep burning sensation was left behind."
    new "疼痛从她的下半身爆发，随之留下的是深处灼烧般的痛感。"

    old "Sarah could feel her whole body move as Matthew drove his finger deeper into her asshole, curling it up, twisting it."
    new "莎拉感觉到马修将手指更深地插入她的肛门，并向上卷曲、扭转，带动她整个身体随之颤动。"

    old "Tears sprung from her face."
    new "泪水涌出她的眼眶。"

    old "She gritted her teeth, lest she scream out."
    new "她咬紧牙关，以免尖叫出声。"

    old "She heard him spit, then felt the spit hit between the cheeks of her ass."
    new "她听见他吐口水，接着感觉到唾液落在了她的臀瓣之间。"

    old "Suddenly, he plunged in another finger."
    new "突然，他又插进了一根手指。"

    old "Sarah screamed out at the surprise spike in pain."
    new "莎拉因突如其来的剧痛而尖叫出声。"

    old "Aided by the lubricant of the spit, Sarah felt his two fingers plunging in and out of her ass."
    new "在唾液的润滑下，莎拉感觉到他的两根手指在她的肛门里进进出出。"

    old "Then, as sudden as it had started, it stopped."
    new "紧接着，就像它突然开始一样，它突然停止了。"

    old "She felt him pull his fingers out of her ass."
    new "她感觉到他把手指从她的肛门里抽了出来。"

    old "Sarah collapsed forward onto the table."
    new "莎拉向前扑倒在桌子上。"

    old "Sorry about that. Thought for a moment I felt something. Had to make sure it was nothing."
    new "抱歉，刚才那一下。我好像感觉到了什么，得确认下没事。"

    old "Sarah slowly pushed herself back up."
    new "莎拉慢慢把自己撑了起来。"

    old "She tried to sit back down, but a sharp pain in her ass caused her flinch and stay standing."
    new "她试图重新坐下，但臀部一阵剧痛让她猛地一缩，只好继续站着。"

    old "Looking at Matthew, she only saw a self-content smile on his face like this was business as usual."
    new "看着马修，她只看到他脸上带着一种自满的微笑，仿佛这一切都是平常事。"

    old "Perhaps, she realized, for him it was."
    new "或许，她意识到，对他来说确实如此。"

    old "Sarah thought about covering herself up again, but after having been prodded everywhere by him, it seemed a waste of time."
    new "莎拉想着再次把自己遮起来，但既然已经被他到处戳弄过了，这似乎是在浪费时间。"

    old "So, these are your uniforms."
    new "所以，这些就是你的制服。"

    old "Sarah watched as Matthew threw a pair of rags down at her feet."
    new "莎拉看着马修将一堆破布扔在她脚边。"

    old "They were clothes, technically."
    new "严格来说，那是衣服。"

    old "Sarah began putting them on."
    new "莎拉开始穿上它们。"

    old "The fabric was coarse and brushed roughly up against her skin."
    new "布料粗糙，摩擦着她的肌肤。"

    old "Compard to the soft fabrics of her dress, these clothes were significantly worse."
    new "与她那件裙子的柔软面料相比，这些衣服要糟糕得多。"

    old "Then again, she imagined her dress probably cost more than a thousand pairs of these prison uniforms."
    new "不过，她心想，她那件裙子恐怕比一千套这样的囚服加起来还贵。"

    old "Fits you like a glove."
    new "穿在你身上正合适。"

    old "Follow along and I'll get you situated, grab that basket of supplies and I'll get you situated."
    new "跟着我，我会安顿好你。去拿那个补给篮子，我来安排你的住处。"

    old "Sarah grabbed the basket and followed Matthew. Doing what he told her seemed like the easiest thing to do for now."
    new "莎拉拿起篮子，跟在马修身后。眼下看来，照他说的做是最省事的选择。"

    old "Leaving the small room, they entered into what appeared to be the main hall."
    new "离开那间小房间后，他们进入了看似主厅的地方。"

    old "The cold grey stone and heavy metal bars drowned out any hint of life."
    new "冰冷的灰色石头和沉重的铁栏掩盖了任何生命的迹象。"

    old "From the corner of her eyes, Sarah spotted a few women leaning up against a wall."
    new "莎拉眼角瞥见几个女人靠在墙边。"

    old "Their eyes followed her as she walked through the hall."
    new "她们的目光跟随着她穿过大厅。"

    old "This is the west wing, your section."
    new "这里是西翼，你的活动区域。"

    old "You stay here, for pretty much most of your stay."
    new "你大部分时间都待在这儿。"

    old "Keep up and I'll show you your cell."
    new "跟上，我带你去看你的牢房。"

    old "Stone. That was about all that could be said for it."
    new "石头。关于它，大概也就只能这么说。"

    old "Sarah looked around. The room was almost disorienting in its uniformity. Endless grey stone."
    new "莎拉环顾四周。这个房间因其千篇一律而令人几乎产生眩晕感。无尽的灰色石头。"

    old "Off to the sides of the room were some beds, or more accurately, piles of hay with a rag for cover."
    new "房间两侧放着几张床，或者更准确地说，是几堆铺着破布的干草。"

    old "Sarah began to realize just how far she was from her comfortable life."
    new "莎拉开始意识到，自己离舒适的生活已经有多远。"

    old "So, you share this cell with another inmate, you're both responsible for the upkeep."
    new "既然你们两人共用这间牢房，那么无论实际过错在谁，维护它的整洁都是你们共同的责任。"

    old "You fail to keep a clean cell that's on the both of you, no matter whose fault it actually is."
    new "不管到底是谁的错，保持牢房清洁是你们两个人的责任。"

    old "Matt gestured towards a bucket in the corner."
    new "马修指了指角落里的一个桶子。"

    old "You got any natural urges, that's the bucket you can use."
    new "有生理需求的话，那个桶就能用。"

    old "Disgusting, was the only thought that came to her."
    new "令她脑海中浮现的只有一个念头：恶心。"

    old "Where do we leave it to be disposed of?"
    new "我们把它放在哪里处理？"

    old "No hotel service here I'm afraid."
    new "恐怕这里没有酒店服务。"

    old "You're responsible for cleaning out your own bucket."
    new "你得自己负责清理你的桶。"

    old "Sarah realized just how foolish she had been for even thinking that someone else would do it for her."
    new "莎拉意识到自己之前指望别人代劳的想法是多么愚蠢。"

    old "Whose my cellmate?"
    new "我的室友是谁？"

    old "Matthew looked around."
    new "马修环顾四周。"

    old "Her name is Eula, but I don't see here anywhere at the moment. Probably playing bone dice or something."
    new "她叫尤拉，不过我现在没看见她。大概是在玩骨骰子之类的游戏吧。"

    old "It's not allowed, technically, but we allow the prisoners some degree of freedom as an incentive to behave."
    new "严格来说是不允许的，但为了激励囚犯们遵守纪律，我们允许他们拥有一定程度的自由。"

    old "Step out of line and you'll be surprised just how fast those priviledges can vanish."
    new "越界的话，你会惊讶于这些特权消失得有多快。"

    old "Sarah nodded, showing him she understood."
    new "莎拉点了点头，表示她明白了。"

    old "Good. Well, that's it then. Go ahead and settle in."
    new "很好。那就这样吧，去安顿下来吧。"

    old "Remember the rules. No fights, no drugs, no trouble. Keep to that, and we'll be fast friends."
    new "记住规矩。不准打架，不准吸毒，不准惹事。只要守规矩，咱们就是好朋友。"

    old "If you got any questions...honestly, ask your cellmate. I'm busy enough as it is."
    new "要是你有什么问题……老实说，去问你的室友吧。我现在的麻烦已经够多了。"

    old "Matthew walked away without saying anything else."
    new "马修一言不发地走开了。"

    old "All of a sudden, Sarah was alone in the cell."
    new "莎拉突然独自一人在牢房里。"

    old "The room was creepy enough when it was the both of them, but all alone, it felt like a tomb."
    new "房间在两人同在时就已经够阴森了，但如今只剩她孤身一人，感觉简直像座坟墓。"

    old "She put her basket off in the corner next to the bed that seemed unused."
    new "她把篮子放在床边的角落里，那张床看起来没人用过。"

    old "Slowly unpacking, she began to take account of what she now owned in life."
    new "她慢慢收拾好行李，开始清点自己如今拥有的身外之物。"

    old "A bar of soap. Some towels. Toiletries."
    new "一块肥皂。几条毛巾。洗漱用品。"

    old "That was essentially all of it. From a princess, down to this."
    new "基本上就这些了。从一位公主，沦落到如此境地。"

    old "Sarah shook her head, how could she have been so stupid to trust Alaric of all people."
    new "莎拉摇了摇头，自己怎么会那么蠢，竟然去信任阿拉里克。"

    old "Suddenly, she heard a sound behind her."
    new "突然，她听到身后传来一阵声响。"

    old "As Sarah turned her head, she saw a woman standing in the door opening, leaning against the side."
    new "莎拉转过头，看见一个女人站在门口，倚在门框上。"

    old "For a moment, she said nothing."
    new "片刻间，她一言不发。"

    old "Sarah was too unsure to speak."
    new "莎拉犹豫不决，不敢开口。"

    old "Finally, the woman did."
    new "终于，那个女人开口了。"

    old "Who the fuck are you, and what are you doing in my cell?"
    new "你他妈到底是谁，在我牢房里干什么？"

    old "I'm...my name is...Sarah."
    new "我……我叫……莎拉。"

    old "Sarah did her best to sound confident, but she realized she was failing."
    new "莎拉尽力让自己听起来自信，但她意识到自己失败了。"

    old "Well, Sarah, how about you fuck back off to your own cell?"
    new "好吧，莎拉，你不如滚回你自己的牢房去？"

    old "This...this is my cell..."
    new "这……这是我的牢房……"

    old "For a moment, the woman looked confused."
    new "有那么一瞬间，这个女人露出了困惑的神情。"

    old "I thought Matt had been fuckin with me, but I really was gettin a new cellmate."
    new "我还以为马特在耍我，没想到我真有个新狱友了。"

    old "The woman's attitude seemed to change. She walked over and extended a hand to Sarah."
    new "女人的态度似乎发生了变化。她走上前，向莎拉伸出了手。"

    old "Eager for some normal human contact, Sarah took her hand."
    new "渴望得到正常的人际接触，莎拉握住了她的手。"

    old "Well, Sarah, my name is Eula."
    new "好吧，莎拉，我叫尤拉。"

    old "Ooh, yes! Matthew told me about you."
    new "哦，是的！马修跟我提起过你。"

    old "What did he tell you?"
    new "他都跟你说了什么？"

    old "Nothing much really, only that we'll be cellmates."
    new "其实也没说什么，只是说我们会成为室友。"

    old "Eula smiled."
    new "尤拉微微一笑。"

    old "Sorry about that whole fuck you routine from before."
    new "抱歉之前对你那么凶。"

    old "I saw a new face and I thought I had to make an impression on you, but if we're cellmates, no need for all that tough actin bullshit."
    new "我刚看到一张新面孔，以为得给你点颜色看看，但既然咱们是狱友，那些装狠的废话就没必要了。"

    old "It's fine, I'm sure it must have been a surprise for you to just find me here."
    new "没关系，我猜你突然在这里发现我，肯定吓了一跳。"

    old "Eula stood back and observed Sarah for a moment, her eyes gliding up and down all of Sarah's body."
    new "尤拉退后一步，打量着莎拉，目光在她全身上下扫视了一遍。"

    old "Not to be a bitch or anything...but...are you sure you're supposed to be here?"
    new "我不是想当个泼妇什么的……但是……你确定你应该待在这儿吗？"

    old "I...Matthew showed me here...I think so..."
    new "是……马修带我来的……我想是的……"

    old "Eula laughed."
    new "尤拉笑了。"

    old "Yeah, I'm sure you're supposed to be here, but I mean more like, in general."
    new "嗯，我确定你确实该在这儿，但我说的不是这个，我是说，从整体来看。"

    old "You don't strike me as the criminal type."
    new "你看起来不像个罪犯。"

    old "Well...I guess I'm not...but I was guilty of a crime, so it's all the same I guess."
    new "嗯……我想我确实不是那种人……但我确实犯过罪，所以结果都一样吧。"

    old "I helped a guy pickpocket in a market...and then I stood up for him, but he gave me up to the guards."
    new "我帮一个小偷在集市上扒窃……后来我还替他出头，结果他却向守卫告发了我。"

    old "Eula sighed."
    new "尤拉叹了口气。"

    old "Fuckin men. They make a mess of it and we ladies get to take the fall, ain't that the truth."
    new "该死的男人。他们把事情搞得一团糟，最后还得我们女人来背锅，可不是嘛。"

    old "Sarah smiled and nodded along. She was mostly just happy to meet a friendly face."
    new "莎拉微笑着点头。她主要是很高兴能遇到一个友善的面孔。"

    old "What are you in for."
    new "你因为什么进来的。"

    old "Look, newbie, don't go around askin people why they're in here for."
    new "听着，菜鸟，别到处问别人为什么坐牢。"

    old "Most of the times you just get into trouble."
    new "大多数时候，你只是会给自己惹上麻烦。"

    old "But you asked me."
    new "但你问了我。"

    old "Eula nodded."
    new "尤拉点了点头。"

    old "Yeah, cause you so fresh-faced you'd actually tell me."
    new "是啊，毕竟你看起来这么青涩天真，还真会老老实实告诉我。"

    old "But look, I'm decent enough, but some of these ladies on the block are pretty bad, so really wanna keep your head down."
    new "不过你看，我人还算本分，但这街上有些女人可不怎么样，所以真的得低调点。"

    old "Especially lookin the way you do, troubles bound to find ya."
    new "尤其是看你这样一副模样，麻烦肯定找上门。"

    old "Eula paused for a moment."
    new "尤拉停顿了一下。"

    old "Anyway, I'm here for a simple shoplifting charge. Third offense, so they gave it to be bad, couple of years, but nothin I can't handle."
    new "总之，我只是因为简单的商店行窃罪被捕。这是第三次了，所以判得重了些，大概两年左右，但这对我来说不算什么难事。"

    old "Sarah was happy to hear it was something trivial."
    new "莎拉听到这不过是件小事，感到很高兴。"

    old "What did you mean when you said some of the women here are bad? I thought everyone in this block was here for small crimes?"
    new "你刚才说这里有些女人很坏，是什么意思？我以为这个监区里的人都是因为小罪进来的。"

    old "Who told you that?"
    new "谁告诉你的？"

    old "Sarah paused before answering, hesitant."
    new "莎拉在回答前停顿了一下，显得有些犹豫。"

    old "Matthew. He told me this wing was pretty safe, no fights."
    new "马修。他告诉我这层楼相当安全，没有打斗。"

    old "Look, you're gonna need to learn to split the real stuff from the bullshit, ok?"
    new "听着，你得学会把真话和屁话分开，明白吗？"

    old "Matthew is the warden for this section, and wants to be warden for the whole prison one day."
    new "马修是这区的典狱长，而且他有一天想当整个监狱的典狱长。"

    old "Well, only way you get to be the big warden is if you can show you're doing a good job."
    new "嗯，想当上大狱长，唯一的办法就是拿出成绩证明你干得不错。"

    old "And the way you show that is by presenting good numbers."
    new "而你要证明这一点，就得拿出漂亮的数据。"

    old "Matthew don't give a fuck if some girl gets her head bashed in, and trust me, plenty do."
    new "马修根本不在乎有没有女孩脑袋被砸碎，相信我，这种事多的是。"

    old "Only thing Matthew cares about is if anyone files a report."
    new "马修唯一在乎的就是有没有人提交报告。"

    old "And most of the time, the person filing the report gets in trouble, not the person that actually started shit."
    new "而且大多数时候，去举报的人反而会惹上麻烦，而不是那个真正惹事的人。"

    old "Eula looked around, making sure nobody else was listening."
    new "尤拉环顾四周，确认没有别人在听。"

    old "And as for some of the women, people are here for the crimes they got caught at, not the crimes they did."
    new "至于有些女人，人们是因为被抓现行而受罚，而不是因为她们犯下的罪行。"

    old "Big difference between the two."
    new "这两者之间差别很大。"

    old "So some of these women on the block are real hard hitters that just got snatched on the only charge that would stick."
    new "所以这街区里有些女人可是狠角色，她们被抓只是因为那个最能坐实的罪名。"

    old "Sarah could understand what Eula was saying. She wanted to hit herself in the head for not realizing it sooner."
    new "莎拉能理解尤拉的意思。她真想给自己一巴掌，恨自己怎么现在才反应过来。"

    old "LOCKDOWN IN FIVE!"
    new "封锁还有五分钟！"

    old "A man's voice could be heard roaring through the hall."
    new "一个男人的声音在走廊里咆哮着回荡。"

    old "Well, you heard the man, celldoors are gonna get locked in five minutes."
    new "好吧，你听到那个人的话了，牢门五分钟后就要锁上。"

    old "When do they open again?"
    new "他们什么时候再开门？"

    old "Eula shrugged."
    new "尤拉耸了耸肩。"

    old "Early next morning, about breakfast time."
    new "第二天一早，差不多是吃早饭的时候。"

    old "Not much light here, so time can get a bit weird, but you catch on after a while."
    new "这儿光线太暗，时间感会有点混乱，不过待久了就习惯了。"

    old "Before long, Sarah heard the sound of the metal door to their cell being locked."
    new "没过多久，莎拉听到了他们牢房金属门被锁上的声音。"

    old "Suddenly, this small room and Eula became her entire world."
    new "突然，这个狭小的房间和尤拉成了她的整个世界。"

    old "I'll walk you around the block tomorrow, show you all the spots, let you know whose cool and who to avoid."
    new "明天我带你去周围转转，给你介绍各个地方，让你知道哪些人不错，哪些人要避开。"

    old "Sarah smiled at Eula."
    new "莎拉对尤拉笑了笑。"

    old "Thank you, Eula. You're maybe the one nice person I've met today."
    new "谢谢你，尤拉。你可能是我今天遇到的唯一好人。"

    old "I was a newbie once and someone taught me, only fair that I return the favor."
    new "我也曾是个新手，有人教过我，现在轮到我回报这份善意了。"

    old "Now go ahead, lay down. You should try to get some rest."
